WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.110
Global navigation satellite systems, often shortened to G N S S, provide position,

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.930
navigation, and timing services.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.720
GPS is one such system.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.270
Drones, vehicles, maps, communications, financial systems, power infrastructure,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.640
and many other technologies depend on satellite-derived position or time.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.210
Jamming is radio-frequency interference that degrades or blocks reception of weak

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.120
satellite-navigation signals.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.760
It may cause lost lock, poor accuracy, warnings,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.440
or failure of features that depend on position.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.619
Interference can be intentional, accidental, local, or caused by equipment faults.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:35.590
Spoofing is deceptive signal manipulation intended to make a receiver calculate an

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.866
incorrect position or time.

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:40.695
A receiver may continue reporting a confident-looking solution even though that solution

00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:42.220
disagrees with reality.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.235
These definitions describe effects, not a field diagnosis.

00:00:45.235 --> 00:00:49.450
Poor sky view, reflected signals, urban canyons, antenna problems, receiver faults,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.660
compass interference, software issues, or stale maps can create similar symptoms.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.730
One unusual reading does not prove an attack.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.960
For drone operators, the immediate question is not who caused the anomaly.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.090
It is whether navigation, automation, logs,

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:05.160
and situational awareness remain trustworthy enough for safe flight and recovery.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.600
This course is defensive only.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.675
Never transmit interference or deceptive navigation signals.

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:12.880
The goal is to understand dependencies, recognize suspicious behavior,

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.900
reduce reliance on uncertain automation, protect people and property, preserve evidence,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.830
and report through appropriate channels.
